<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's Bucaram to address nation on strike.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's Bucaram to address nation on strike.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's President Abdala Bucaram will address the nation by television and radio Tuesday on the subject of the 48-hour general strike scheduled for Wednesday, presidential spokesmen said.</p>
<p>The address will begin at 2030 local time (0130 Wednesday GMT), they said.</p>
<p>The strike is the latest action in a wave of protests against Bucaram's young government and its austerity measures, which have included steep increases in the costs of public services.</p>
<p>((-- Quito Newsroom +5932 25-8429))</p>
